&lt;h2 id="the-story"&gt;The Story&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I was editing one of my server listings on the platform when I intercepted the PATCH request in Burp Suite. Something caught my eye — the request body already contained an &lt;code&gt;imageUrls&lt;/code&gt; parameter, sitting there empty alongside other fields:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;data=test&amp;amp;imageUrls=[]&amp;amp;...
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;According to the UI, uploading images was &lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;Premium Only&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; — the frontend showed a clear message: &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;Uploading images is only available to premium servers.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>